  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1216 AM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nA ridge of high pressure will continue to provide abundant sunshine \nwith ample dry weather conditions over the next seven days. The H5 \nridge axis nudges more east on Saturday with heights peaking at 588 \ndm. This translates to daily light northeasterly winds shifting \nsoutherly on Saturday, only resulting in a subtle increase in WAA. \nDaily temperatures will remain near to slightly above normal in the \nmid to upper 70s, with lows ranging from the mid to upper 40s. \nOtherwise, patchy fog near bodies of water will remain possible this \nmorning. The only other weather concern is a 15% chance of a \nsprinkle or isolated rain shower on Tuesday afternoon as a cold\nfront washes out over the FA. While a 0% PoP is currently \nprogged by the NBM, model ensembles support at least a slight \nmention.",
